# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key.
# .env.local is gitignored -- never commit real keys.

# Used for semantic dedup and gap analysis's embedding comparisons
# (flowscout/embeddings.py, flowscout/semantic_dedup.py,
# flowscout/gap_analysis.py). Without any of the three keys below,
# FlowScout still runs fine -- it just falls back to structural dedup
# only, and gap analysis reports every TCMS item as not_found instead of
# comparing by meaning (see semantic_dedup_status / gap status in a
# run's flows.json / report).
#
# Pick ONE provider (set "embeddings_provider" in your config JSON, or
# the web UI's New Run form, to match) and set that provider's key --
# the other two can stay blank. Gemini is the default if
# embeddings_provider isn't set at all.
#
# Gemini's integration has been exercised against real API calls
# throughout this project's development. Currently the only usable
# provider (see embeddings.py's module docstring and ROADMAP.md's
# "Embeddings provider" entry for the full story).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI (text-embedding-3-small) -- code paused/commented out in
# embeddings.py (Aug 2026): a live key confirmed valid via GET
# /v1/models, but the embeddings call itself hit 429 insufficient_quota
# (an account billing issue, not a code bug) before the response-parsing
# path could be verified. Setting this env var currently has no effect
# until the provider is re-enabled in embeddings.py.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Voyage AI (voyage-3.5) -- code paused/commented out in embeddings.py,
# no live check at all yet. Anthropic's own recommended embeddings
# partner (Anthropic has no embeddings model of its own). Setting this
# env var currently has no effect until the provider is re-enabled.
VOYAGE_API_KEY=
